"The lme4 package for R provides replacements lmer and nlmer for the lme 
and nlme functions in the nlme package. The new package allows useRs to 
fit linear mixed models or generalized linear mixed models or nonlinear 
mixed models with multiple levels of random effects in nested or crossed 
or partially crossed configurations. The underlying computational 
methods provide the ability to work with very large data sets, such as 
are encountered in a value-added analysis of standardized test scores in 
education research, without sacrificing efficiency in smaller models.

