Kyong

My question: 

Hello, Splus users,

 I generated a residual vs fitted graph from a regression. One of the 

 independent variables has '1" and "2" for specifying  two groups. I 

 want to mark the points with 1 or 2 to identify the points.

 I appreciate your help very much.

 Kyong

From: Richard:

tmp <- data.frame(yhat=rnorm(12),

                  resid=rnorm(12),

                  group=factor(rep(c("a","b"),6))) xyplot(resid ~ yhat, groups=group, data="" panel=panel.superpose) xyplot(resid ~ yhat, groups=group, data="" panel=panel.superpose, pch=c("a","b")) xyplot(resid ~ yhat, groups=group, data="" panel=panel.superpose, pch=c("1","2"))

>From Vivek:

Hello Kyong,

In R you would use identify() to accomplish this. You can read the help page, but the basic idea is to pass it a list of your points (so that when you click on the graph it can find them) and a list of labels (optional) so that it knows what to write on the graph. Try it, and if you need more help, let us know!

Vivek

