Speed of ‘roll’ is highly
dependent on the complexity of the function itself.

A 500-step backtesting of a multivariate garch
(which is computationally intensive) can take up to 10min on my humble 2.4GHz, 1GB
Ram desktop.

But I feel this to be an acceptable speed
for the wealth of the returned statistics.

I guess the main virtue of the function is
in its flexibility rather than its speed.

I am pretty sure you could roll faster if
you called your GLMs with C, but that is an entirely different story…

 

 

