References: <20060425234547.35887100955A@mailgate.biostat.wustl.edu>
Message-ID: <444EBFAF.807@blackmesacapital.com>

To answer your first question, use seriesData() to extract the vector or 
matrix of data from a timeSeries or signalSeries object.

To combine colums of multiple timeSeries, use the function seriesMerge():

> A <- timeSeries(1:3, pos=1:3)
> B <- timeSeries(cbind(B1=4:6, B2=7:9), pos=1:3)
> A
  Positions 1
 1960/01/02 1
 1960/01/03 2
 1960/01/04 3
> B
  Positions B1 B2
 1960/01/02 4  7
 1960/01/03 5  8
 1960/01/04 6  9
> seriesData(A)
[1] 1 2 3
> seriesMerge(A, B)
  Positions 1 B1 B2
 1960/01/02 1 4  7
 1960/01/03 2 5  8
 1960/01/04 3 6  9
> X <- seriesMerge(A, B)
> colIds(seriesData(X))[1] <- "A"
> X
  Positions A B1 B2
 1960/01/02 1 4  7
 1960/01/03 2 5  8
 1960/01/04 3 6  9
>

